// Copyright (c) 2026 Eleftherios Notas and The XIOM Authors
// Licensed under the MIT or Apache-2.0 license, at your option.
//
// DESIGN: vendored path (Vulkan SDK exports no SPIRV-Reflect DLL; its
// SPIRV.dll is a stub with a single non-reflect export). The upstream
// spirv_reflect.{h,c} + include/spirv/unified1/spirv.h are vendored verbatim
// into vendor/ (byte-pinned, per-file SHA256 in SPEC.md section 2) and
// compiled in C with the suite via port.args.json; src/spvref_bridge.c adds
// the `xspv_*` probe surface. This is the ONLY module in the package with
// `extern "C"` (G5).
//
// COVERAGE: 45 functions (100% of the spvReflect* C API; oracle = committed
// parser tools/oracle_spvreflect.py over vendor/spirv_reflect.h) plus 186
// enum/macro values bound as `pub const`.
//
// ABI discipline (B-11..B-20): probe out-params are XIOM-owned byte slots the
// bridge writes little-endian; strings are copied INTO owned slots by C and
// read back byte-indexed (B-20 -- XIOM never reads through a foreign
// pointer); no raw pointer arithmetic anywhere; one owned slot per out-param.
//
// The raw extern surface maps size_t/uint32_t -> Int/Int32 and every pointer
// to Int (0 = NULL). Struct-by-value never crosses: reflection structs stay
// in the bridge and only scalar fields / copied strings come back.

module xiom.spirvreflect

use xiom.encoding;

// =========================================================================
// Oracle constants -- all 186 enum/macro values from vendor/spirv_reflect.h
// (source-generated by tools/oracle_spvreflect.py emit-consts; regenerate
// after a re-pin and diff against this block).
// =========================================================================

